<resources>

    <!-- Base application theme. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <!-- Customize your theme here. -->
        <item name="android:editTextBackground">@drawable/rn_edit_text_material</item>
        <!-- Was unset, so the very first frame before RN/JS loads fell back
             to Theme.AppCompat.DayNight's own default background — near-black
             in dark mode, which is what showed up as a black splash screen.
             Pinned to the brand blue so it's consistent regardless of the
             device's light/dark setting. -->
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
    </style>

    <!-- MainActivity's post-splash theme — paints the branded logo-on-blue
         (see main_activity_window_background.xml) for the brief window
         after the system splash is dismissed but before RN's JS has
         actually rendered a first frame. This is no longer MainActivity's
         manifest theme directly — see Theme.App.SplashScreen, which hands
         off to this one. -->
    <style name="AppTheme.Main">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/main_activity_window_background</item>
    </style>

    <!-- Explicit Android SplashScreen API (API 31+, back-ported to older
         versions by androidx.core:core-splashscreen) config for MainActivity
         — see AndroidManifest.xml (this is set as MainActivity's theme) and
         MainActivity.kt's installSplashScreen() call. Without this, the OS
         is *required* to show its own system splash screen on API 31+
         (targetSdkVersion is 36) and auto-derives the icon from the app's
         launcher icon with its own padding assumptions — that auto
         derivation was what rendered the logo blown up edge-to-edge/cropped
         in the first place.

         BUG FIX, ROUND 3 (product report: logo STILL rendering too large
         after two separate fixes to main_activity_window_background.xml —
         the drawable AppTheme.Main/postSplashScreenTheme below actually
         uses). Both those fixes targeted the wrong phase: this comment
         previously assumed leaving windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon unset
         meant "no icon at all" here, but that's not how the SplashScreen
         API actually behaves — omitting it doesn't suppress an icon, it
         makes the system fall back to auto-deriving one from the app's
         own launcher icon (AndroidManifest.xml's android:icon), applying
         its own padding/masking assumptions — the exact "blown up/
         cropped" auto-derivation problem this whole custom splash setup
         was built to avoid in the first place, just never actually
         avoided for THIS specific phase. That's what was still rendering
         too large this whole time, regardless of how correct
         main_activity_window_background.xml's own sizing became — this
         phase's own auto-derived icon was never touched by either
         previous fix.

         Explicitly setting windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon to a fully
         transparent placeholder (splash_transparent_icon.xml) is what
         actually suppresses the automatic fallback: the system now has
         an icon it was explicitly given, so it never substitutes its
         own auto-derived one — this phase now genuinely shows nothing
         but the plain background color, which was always the intent.
         It's brief regardless (this phase ends the moment MainActivity's
         window is ready to draw), and postSplashScreenTheme immediately
         hands off to AppTheme.Main below, which shows the actual logo at
         a size fully controlled via a plain windowBackground drawable. -->
    <style name="Theme.App.SplashScreen" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_transparent_icon</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.Main</item>
    </style>

</resources>
